# Documentation & prompt language

All project memory and agent control surfaces are written in **English**.

## Scope (must be English)

- Everything under `.ai/` — including `progress.md`, specs, plans, tasks,
  ADRs, glossary, lessons, and README.
- Everything under `.cursor/` — rules, commands, skills, hooks docs, and
  verify-related notes that are human/agent prose.

New or edited files in those trees use English. Do not add new Spanish (or
other) prose there.

## Out of scope (unchanged)

- Product UI copy and locale files (`es` / `en` dictionaries, route path
  segments like `catalogo`, storefront/backoffice strings). Those follow
  product i18n rules, not this rule.
- Historical Spanish already in `.ai/` or `.cursor/` may remain until
  deliberately rewritten; when you touch a section, prefer rewriting that
  section in English rather than extending Spanish.
- Exception: `.ai/progress.md` is fully English (token-sensitive handoff).
  Keep new progress entries in English and concise.

## Prompts

User and agent prompts for this project are in English from now on. Reply and
plan in English unless the user explicitly asks for another language for a
single reply.
